To run the C compiler:
	g++ -o loop loop.cpp
To run the program:
	./loop
To see the assembly listing:
	g++ -c -S loop.cpp
To see the assembly listing with debug:
	g++ -g -c -S loop.cpp
To see the assembly listing with debug and optimization:
	g++ -g -c -S -O3 loop.cpp
To see the assembly listing without debug and with optimization:
	g++ -c -S -O3 loop.cpp

You should see the optimizer remove all unnecessary code (the loop)
when you use the last command.
